# Local-dev defaults for the Go backend. `godotenv` loads `.env` on startup
# (see internal/config/config.go), so copy this to `.env` and adjust if your
# local Postgres isn't on the default port/credentials. See
# apps/backend/scripts/setup-dev-db.sql for the matching bootstrap.

POSTGRES_URL=postgres://kaata:kaata_dev@localhost:5432/kaata?sslmode=disable
BACKEND_PORT=8080

# Target of the /v1/download redirect. In local dev we point at the Vite
# dev server which serves apps/web/public/downloads/ at root. The web
# button hits the backend's /v1/download which 302s to this URL.
APK_DOWNLOAD_URL=http://localhost:3000/downloads/kaata-0.1.0.apk

# Soft-migration signal. When set, every check-in response carries this URL
# in the `migrate_to_backend_url` field. Mobile clients persist it locally
# and switch to it on their next launch. Use this to move the backend to a
# new domain without forcing users to reinstall.
#   - Leave empty (or unset): no migration signal — clients stay on the
#     URL they were built with (EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL).
#   - Set to "https://new.example.com": clients migrate to that URL.
#   - Set to "" (empty string) explicitly: clears any prior override on
#     clients, reverting them to their build-time default.
# MIGRATE_TO_BACKEND_URL=

# Google OAuth web client ID. This is the AUDIENCE we validate against
# when verifying mobile-supplied Google ID tokens at /v1/auth/google.
# Get it from https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials — the
# "Web application" OAuth client (NOT the Android one). Public value;
# not a secret. The corresponding client *secret* is unused by us.
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# HMAC secret for signing the session JWT we issue to mobile clients after
# a successful Google sign-in. Generate via `openssl rand -hex 32`. MUST
# be a long random string — anything short makes brute force feasible.
# Rotating invalidates every currently-issued session.
SESSION_JWT_SECRET=
